This is a brilliant addition. Fetching the official date from the backend ensures data integrity, while the boolean "twist" gives you the flexibility to turn manual overrides on or off in the future without rewriting code.
Here are the exact blocks to replace in **JournalBulkUpload.js** to fetch the date from the API and lock the calendar based on your boolean.
### 1. Update State & useEffect (Combine EOD and Date Fetching)
We will add the boolean flag and combine the EOD check and Date fetch into a single initial load function.
**Find your existing useEffect block (around line 140) and replace it entirely with this:**
```javascript
  const [isCreatingBatch, setIsCreatingBatch] = useState(false);
  const [batchCreated, setBatchCreated] = useState(false); 
  const [isPageLoading, setIsPageLoading] = useState(true);
  const [isEodRunning, setIsEodRunning] = useState(false);

  // --- NEW: The "Twist" Boolean ---
  // Set to true to allow manual date changes. Set to false to strictly lock it to the API date.
  const allowManualDateSelection = false; 

  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchInitialData = async () => {
      try {
        setIsPageLoading(true);
        
        // 1. Check EOD Status First
        const eodResponse = await callApi("/JS/journals/eod_status", null, "GET");
        if (eodResponse && Array.isArray(eodResponse) && eodResponse.length > 0) {
          if (eodResponse[0].eodStatus === 1) {
            setIsEodRunning(true);
            return; // Stop loading anything else, block the screen
          }
        }

        // 2. Fetch the Official Posting Date
        const dateResponse = await callApi("/JS/journals/current-posting-date", null, "GET");
        if (dateResponse) {
          // Parse the YYYY-MM-DD date perfectly into DayJS for the calendar
          const parsedDate = dayjs(dateResponse, "YYYY-MM-DD");
          if (parsedDate.isValid()) {
            setSelectedDate(parsedDate);
          } else {
            showSnackBar("Failed to parse official posting date.", "error");
          }
        } else {
          showSnackBar("Failed to load official posting date.", "error");
        }

      } catch (error) {
        console.error("Failed to fetch initial data:", error);
      } finally {
        setIsPageLoading(false);
      }
    };

    fetchInitialData();
  }, [callApi, showSnackBar]);

```
### 2. Update resetAll to Preserve the API Date
Currently, when a user clicks the "Reset" icon after a successful upload, it wipes the date blank. If manual selection is blocked, we want the API date to stay perfectly in place so they can upload another file immediately.
**Find your resetAll function (around line 245) and replace it with this:**
```javascript
  const resetAll = () => {
    setActiveStep(0);
    setRequestId(null);
    setResultStatus(null);
    setValidationStage(0);
    setResultMsg("");
    setPreviewRows([]);
    setTotalRows(0);
    setIsProcessing(false);
    setAutoDlTriggered(false);
    setIsCsvFile(false);
    setIsErrorDownloaded(false);
    
    // --- THIS CLEARS THE SUCCESS BANNER ---
    setBatchCreated(false); 
    
    setFile(null);

    // ONLY clear the date if manual selection is enabled. Otherwise, keep the API date!
    if (allowManualDateSelection) {
      setSelectedDate(null);
    }
    
    setPage(0);
    setDownloadMsg("Downloading error report...");
    clearInput();
  };

```
### 3. Update the <DatePicker> Component
Now we will apply the boolean to the DatePicker. By using readOnly={!allowManualDateSelection}, the calendar still looks perfectly normal and blue, but the user is physically unable to click or open it if the boolean is false.
**Scroll down to your return statement. Find the <DatePicker> component (around line 520) and replace it entirely with this:**
```javascript
                  <DatePicker
                    label="Posting Date"
                    value={selectedDate}
                    onChange={(newValue) => {
                      if (allowManualDateSelection) setSelectedDate(newValue);
                    }}
                    disabled={isProcessing || isCreatingBatch}
                    
                    // --- NEW: Locks the calendar popup if boolean is false ---
                    readOnly={!allowManualDateSelection} 
                    
                    minDate={dayjs().subtract(1, 'year')}
                    maxDate={dayjs()}
                    slotProps={{
                      textField: {
                        size: "small",
                        onKeyDown: (e) => e.preventDefault(),
                        helperText: file && !selectedDate ? "Please select a posting date" : "",
                        FormHelperTextProps: { sx: { color: "primary.main", fontWeight: 500 } },
                        sx: file && !selectedDate ? { "& .MuiOutlinedInput-root": { "& fieldset": { borderColor: "primary.main", borderWidth: "2px" } } } : {},
                        inputProps: { 
                          readOnly: true, 
                          // Cursor turns to an arrow (default) instead of a pointer if locked
                          sx: { cursor: allowManualDateSelection ? 'pointer' : 'default' } 
                        }
                      },
                    }}
                  />

```
